

<h1>Your California Privacy Rights</h1>
<p class="dates">Effective: January 1, 2020<br>Last Updated: August 22, 2025</p>
<p>Pursuant to Section 1798.83 of the California Civil Code, residents of California have the right to request, under certain circumstances, certain information with respect to the types of personal information the business shares with third parties for those third parties' direct marketing purposes and the identities of the third parties with whom the business has shared such information during the immediately preceding calendar year. An individual may make one request per year. To make such a request, please send an email to <a href="mailto:ccpanotice@bluecompassrv.com">ccpanotice@bluecompassrv.com</a> or write to us at:</p>
<div class="addr"><b>CA Privacy Rights</b><br><i>Attn: Marketing Privacy Manager</i><br><b>RV Retailer, LLC</b><br>301 E Las Olas Blvd<br>Suite 700<br>Fort Lauderdale, FL 33301</div>
<p>The California Consumer Privacy Act ("CCPA") also affords California residents certain rights over their personal information (subject to certain exceptions). Our <a href="ccpa-notice.html">CCPA Privacy Notice</a>, which supplements our Privacy Policy, outlines those rights and explains how they may be exercised.</p>
